00:40:00,941 --> 00:40:03,820
It's very similar to a quarter.

467
00:40:03,821 --> 00:40:11,520
It's different types of metals put together, some soft and some harder, to provide a wafer-like

468
00:40:11,521 --> 00:40:19,740
or wave of hard and soft protection that gives it a much better ability to withstand shots.

469
00:40:22,120 --> 00:40:26,140
Despite its 63-ton weight, it is exceptionally mobile.

470
00:40:28,040 --> 00:40:30,520
Boasting the most powerful tank engine ever built,

471
00:40:31,080 --> 00:40:35,060
the Abrams can move at speeds up to 45 miles per hour.

472
00:40:35,880 --> 00:40:40,360
It uses a turbine engine, much the same engine that's used in a helicopter.

473
00:40:40,361 --> 00:40:48,340
this tank can literally be driven at speeds that would cause the track to fall off it were it worked

474
00:40:48,341 --> 00:40:54,160
like a charm we had never had a turbine in a ground application turbine that big 1500 horsepower in a

475
00:40:54,161 --> 00:41:02,200
ground application before as they entered Desert Storm the Abrams tank did battle with Iraq's most

476
00:41:02,201 --> 00:41:08,700
formidable tank the Soviet made T-72

477
00:41:09,740 --> 00:41:15,160
during several dramatic battles US tank crews successfully located and destroyed

478
00:41:15,161 --> 00:41:21,160
enemy tanks before the Iraqis even detected their presence during the Gulf

479
00:41:21,161 --> 00:41:27,420
War one of the nicknames for the Abrams tank was whispering death because it

480
00:41:27,421 --> 00:41:32,760
does not have a tank like sound.

481
00:41:32,761 --> 00:41:36,300
By the end of Desert Storm, Iraqis 4,000 tanks

482
00:41:36,301 --> 00:41:39,120
had been reduced to fewer than 100,

483
00:41:39,121 --> 00:41:43,020
while the US lost only four.

484
00:41:43,021 --> 00:41:49,020
Desert Storm was so quick, so decisive,

485
00:41:49,021 --> 00:41:51,380
that the international community is still

486
00:41:51,381 --> 00:41:55,380
reeling from the impact of this tank.

487
00:41:55,381 --> 00:42:00,560
It was such a quantum leap in capability.

488
00:42:00,561 --> 00:42:04,300
And it brings such great confidence

489
00:42:04,301 --> 00:42:07,440
to this very difficult business that we do.

490
00:42:07,441 --> 00:42:11,400
The best evidence, I guess, that I can cite

491
00:42:11,401 --> 00:42:16,420
was a statement by an Iraqi brigade commander who

492
00:42:16,421 --> 00:42:20,080
said something to this effect, that the United States Air

493
00:42:20,081 --> 00:42:22,420
Force bombed us for three weeks,

494
00:42:22,421 --> 00:42:24,760
and we lost a few tanks and some people.

495
00:42:24,761 --> 00:42:29,640
Then along came the 2nd Cavalry, and we lost the whole brigade in an afternoon.

496
00:42:32,560 --> 00:42:40,880
Due to its success during Desert Storm, the Abrams has convinced many military strategists of the tank's necessity in the modern age.

497
00:42:43,580 --> 00:42:47,440
Mobile protected firepower is what the tank is.

498
00:42:48,080 --> 00:42:51,500
And the tank is the centerpiece of mobile protected firepower.

499
00:42:51,501 --> 00:42:59,400
But the tank is the key to battle success as long as you can foresee it.

500
00:43:00,780 --> 00:43:04,620
It has caused the nature of land warfare to change.

501
00:43:05,680 --> 00:43:13,940
That's what happens whenever you have such a dominant piece of technology introduced into mission and battle.

502
00:43:14,200 --> 00:43:19,200
It causes the nature of warfare to change dramatically.

503
00:43:21,500 --> 00:43:26,520
From the primitive Mark I

504
00:43:26,521 --> 00:43:32,280
to the groundbreaking armored fighting machines of World War II

505
00:43:32,281 --> 00:43:35,960
to the high-tech Abrams,

506
00:43:37,340 --> 00:43:40,200
tanks have helped determine the fate of nations.

507
00:43:41,160 --> 00:43:43,020
Until the next evolution in armor,

508
00:43:43,021 --> 00:43:46,840
